# Exemption list for the causality gate's no-base refusal.
#
# An added test (one this diff declares) that the base run produced no result for - "not run at
# base" - proves nothing on either tree, so `cargo xtask test-causality` now FAILS it unless it is
# exempted here by name. These are the tests that legitimately produce no base result: a
# feature-gated test the reconstruction leaves out, or a test whose module is declared in a file the
# base run reverts.
#
# Format: one test-fn name per line, with a `# reason` required on each line - the reason is the
# only thing a reviewer reads to decide whether the exemption is still earned.
#
#   <test_fn_name> # <why this test produces no base result>
#
# Three shapes are REFUSED rather than silently accepted, so the file stays honest:
#   - a line with no ` # reason`;
#   - a line naming no test this diff added (a stale entry that exempts nothing);
#   - an added test with no base result that is not listed here.
#
# The list below is EMPTY: there are no current no-base exemptions. Add one only when the gate
# names a test you cannot make run at base, and delete it with its reason when it can.
